[0m[0m
[1mstack.rs[22m — Linked-list stack using [38;5;10mOption<Box<ListNode>>[0m. [38;5;10mNone[0m represents empty (replacing the C sentinel node pattern). [38;5;10mpush[0m prepends, [38;5;10mpop[0m removes head, [38;5;10mpeek[0m traverses [38;5;10mpos[0m nodes, [38;5;10mprint[0m walks the list, and [38;5;10mDrop[0m drains all nodes.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mthrow.rs[22m — [38;5;10mmath_err[0m and [38;5;10mop_err[0m print error messages to stderr and call [38;5;10mstd::process::abort()[0m (matching the C behavior of [38;5;10mraise(SIGFPE)[0m / [38;5;10mraise(SIGILL)[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mslothvm.rs[22m — [38;5;10mexecute[0m runs a bytecode interpreter loop matching on opcode bytes (0x00–0x0A). Each opcode manipulates the stack and advances [38;5;10mpc[0m exactly as the C version does, including the tricky OUT case where [38;5;10mpc[0m increments twice (once before the type-code switch, once after).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mparser.rs[22m — [38;5;10mparse[0m reads a [38;5;10m.sloth[0m file line by line, scanning for keywords:[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mslothy[0m → emits [38;5;10m0x01[0m (PUSH)[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msloth[0m → increments a counter (used as operand value)[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mand[0m → emits the current counter as a byte, resets it[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mnap[0m → emits [38;5;10m0x00[0m (EXIT)[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m#[0m starts a comment (rest of line ignored)[0m[0m
- At end of each line with tokens, emits the final counter value[0m[0m
